; Independent AI board review of the Form-native persistent dialogue organ.
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk observe/review-panel.fk observe/review-ask.fk

(ra-review
  "plugin/public-dialogue.fk"
  "Review only; do not edit any file. Inspect plugin/public-dialogue.fk, plugin/chatgpt-plugin.fk, plugin/openapi.json, plugin/ai-plugin.json, plugin/tests/public-dialogue-band.fk, plugin/tests/public-dialogue-restart-witness.fk, plugin/tests/public-dialogue-socket-witness.fk, and plugin/tests/public-dialogue-contract-band.fk. The implementation boundary is no Python and no non-Form application code: fkwu executes every runtime behavior. Freshly preflight and run the Form proofs. Adversarially test persistent root/reply creation, directed-edge reads from either turn, independent per-turn removal capabilities, digest and token non-disclosure, content-free tombstones, restart persistence, HTTP body framing, MCP tools/list and tools/call, malformed inputs, and compatibility with the existing plugin. Return PASS AS A FORM-NATIVE PERSISTENT DIALOGUE, REVISE, or BLOCK. Locate every objection with executable evidence. Empty or unfinished output is absence, not a vote.")
